# JUranometria's English interface language (Sprint 33, issue #348).
#
# This is a SHIPPED RESOURCE and it is the reason English is offered.
# Interface availability is read from the descriptors present in this
# directory - never inferred from the absence of anything, never
# scanned out of Java, and never borrowed from the chart language
# packs next door.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Why a descriptor exists before any translated strings do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# English is currently the only interface language, and today its
# strings live in Java rather than in a resource bundle. It would
# have been less work to let discovery answer "en" when it found no
# descriptors at all. That would have been a mechanism producing the
# right answer for the wrong reason: nobody would learn it had never
# run until a second language was added and failed to appear.
#
# So English registers here like any other interface language would,
# the discovery path is exercised on every build, and #350 populates
# the strings BEHIND this registration without touching availability.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Not a chart language
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The sky's names and the controls' words are two settings a reader
# chooses separately, and this file governs only the second. A chart
# language pack lives under resources/sky-language, declares
# schema=1, and carries a names file; an interface descriptor lives
# here, declares interface-schema=1, and carries no names at all.
# The two indexes have different paths AND different shapes, so
# neither discovery can read the other's - a Norwegian chart pack
# cannot make a Norwegian interface appear, which is the promise the
# reader was given.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Fields
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# interface-schema  the descriptor format, and the marker that keeps
#                   this out of chart discovery
# tag               the language tag; what gets stored in
#                   language.interface
# display-name      what this language calls itself. Descriptor data,
#                   not a policy: whether a selector shows the
#                   autonym or a translated language name is #350's
#                   to decide, and deciding it changes no availability
# strings           where this language's words come from. #350
#                   replaced "in-code" with the file beside this one;
#                   this file's role did not change, which is what
#                   registering English before it had strings was
#                   for

interface-schema=1
tag=en
display-name=English
strings=en.properties
status=complete
